-- title:
--   Stalk dominated by R₂ gives a non-closed point
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$ and a package $\mathfrak{X} : \mathrm{DRModelPackage}\ p$ (which records properness, flatness and integrality of `DRModel.toBase p`, integral closedness of its affine sections, the models of the curve over $\mathbb{Q}$ and over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with their compatibility with the arithmetic Galois action and with places, two sections, and a smooth locus). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, let $K$ be its fraction field and $\iota_K : K \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ a ring map. Write $\mathfrak{X}_O$ for the pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb{Z} \to O$, assumed integral. Given a point $x$ of $\mathfrak{X}_O$ and a ring map $\varphi$ from the function field of $\mathfrak{X}_O$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(1 \cdot p)$, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise image of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\ p$, assume: (hφO) for every $a \in O$, $\varphi$ carries the germ at $x$ of the global section of $\mathfrak{X}_O$ coming from $a$ along the second projection to the image of $\iota_K(a)$ under $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(1 \cdot p)$; (hφj) for every $a$ in the finite chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\ \mathbb{Z}\ (\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\ p)\ (\mathrm{jFull}\ p)$, i.e. every element of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\ p$ integral over $\mathbb{Z}[j]$, the function-field element obtained by pulling $a$ back along the first projection over the preimage of the finite chart (a nonempty open, as assumed) is sent by $\varphi$ to the element whose Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is `coeffEmb` applied to the Laurent series of $a$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let further $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $k$ a perfect, algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, $red : A \to k$ a ring map, $data$ a `ModularPolynomialData` for $p$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence $hKr$, and $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ the integrality hypotheses on the two degeneracy maps at level $1$ and prime $p$; let $P$ be a `PlaceSpecialization` for these data and $R$ a `ProlongationTuple` over $P$, whose component $R_2$ is a regular prolongation of $A$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(1 \cdot p)$ with valuation ring $R_2.\mathrm{integers}$. Assume $\iota_K(\mathrm{image\ of\ }O) \subseteq A$ and that $toκ : O \to k$ is the induced reduction, $toκ(a) = red(\iota_K(a))$. Finally let $c$ be a point of $\mathfrak{X}_O$ lying over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} O$ such that $\varphi$ maps the image in the function field of the whole stalk at $c$ into $R_2.\mathrm{integers}$, and the image of the maximal ideal of that stalk into the non-units of $R_2.\mathrm{integers}$. Then the singleton $\{c\}$ is not closed in $\mathfrak{X}_O$.
--
--   This is the statement that a point of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model over $O$ whose local ring is dominated, through $\varphi$, by the second Gauss-type prolongation ring $R_2$ cannot be a closed point; domination of the maximal ideal into the non-units, and not mere containment of the stalk, is what rules closed points out. It is the $R_2$ half of the centre-identification step used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.mem_integers_and_mem_integers_of_stalk_of_specializes`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.mem_integers_and_mem_integers_of_stalk_of_specializes), where the two prolongations $R_1$ and $R_2$ are located on the two branches of the special fibre.
